{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_slice_5", "label": "Slice 5 \u2014 Drive It From a Browser", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The plan's framing was wrong: this was never an access problem. The api already mounts the blob volume read-write, SourceStore and DerivativeStore read the same file, and WorkerRole is a naming and ownership gate enforced by a grep."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_source_reader", "label": "SourceReader", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Read-only: open(root) with no proof, get, no put, no remove. Relaxing the SourceStore gate instead would hand the api put and remove on source bytes to buy a read, and the write surface is the half of that type worth gating."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_download_route", "label": "GET /api/revisions/{id}/download?variant=original", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "No library segment, matching DATA.md: resolving the library from the revision and then checking it against itself is a no-op that reads like a check, which is worse than no check. Filters part.deleted_at IS NULL so a held URL does not outlive a delete."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_open_path_vs_download", "label": "Download Is Not Open", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The open-path rule is about opening \u2014 the grid, the viewer, the detail card, the path whose budget is 80 ms and whose failure mode is parsing STEP to draw a thumbnail. Download is a distinct, deliberately-named path that streams stored bytes to a user who asked for those exact bytes and parses nothing; the byte-identity product rule cannot be satisfied without it."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_content_disposition_rfc5987", "label": "RFC 5987 Content-Disposition Filename", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Both halves \u2014 an ASCII filename= fallback and filename*=UTF-8'' \u2014 because Turkish part names carry g-breve, s-cedilla and dotless i and a naive filename= mangles the download. The fixture carries a Turkish name rather than an ASCII one with a comment about Turkish."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_rehash_before_serving", "label": "Re-Hash the Bytes Before Serving Them", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "BLAKE3 at ~1 GB/s is free next to the transfer that follows, and it makes the product claim actually true rather than asserted. It also closes the hole ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING leaves: a crash between write_blob's rename and the commit can leave a file with no row, and a later ingest under a different format writes a row whose level does not match those bytes."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_library_storage_panel", "label": "LibraryStorage Totals Panel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A blob-only sum reports 0 B of derivatives for a library where every part has a preview, because thumbnails live inline in derivative.thumb_bytes with no blob row; and summing over file rows rather than distinct blobs double-counts a deduplicated library. The ratio is computed server-side so two consumers cannot report the same library upside down."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_head_touches_last_accessed", "label": "HEAD Warms last_accessed_at", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "axum's get(handler) also routes HEAD and the handler runs to completion before the body is discarded, so a HEAD moves the timestamp while handing nobody any bytes. Both blob.rs and download.rs have the identical shape, so it is a property of both routes rather than a bug in one, and patching a single handler would be the wrong shape of fix."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_check_open_path_boundary", "label": "check_open_path_boundary Grep Gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A green run proves 'nothing named SourceStore directly', not 'no source bytes are reachable'. It gains one assertion per read handle \u2014 SourceReader only in download.rs \u2014 because a handle in one named route is a decision and the same handle in six files is the mistake arrived at by copy-paste."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_zstd_level_is_the_authority", "label": "blob.zstd_level Decides Decompression", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Not Compression::for_source_format, which is ingest-time policy that slice 7 is about to change; a reader that re-derives policy would start returning zstd frames the day the policy moves. A NULL level on a source blob is not 'raw' \u2014 it is 'nobody recorded how these bytes were stored' \u2014 and the route answers 500 naming the blob rather than falling through to a hash mismatch that explains nothing."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_recompression_ordering_constraint", "label": "Forward Constraint \u2014 Row First, Then Bytes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "In-place recompression rewrites bytes and updates zstd_level with no transaction spanning both. Row-first shows level 3 over raw bytes, which fails loudly; bytes-first shows level 0 over a zstd frame and would return the frame as if it were the file. Slice 7 writes the row first, or sniffs frame magic; picking neither is not an option."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_slice_5", "target": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_4_derivatives_design_slice_4", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_download_route", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_source_reader", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_download_route", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_rehash_before_serving", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_download_route", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_content_disposition_rfc5987", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_download_route", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_zstd_level_is_the_authority", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_download_route", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_open_path_vs_download", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_check_open_path_boundary", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_source_reader", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_check_open_path_boundary", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_source_store", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_source_reader", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_source_store", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_01_phase_0a_foundation_design_lapidary_api", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_download_route", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_01_phase_0a_foundation_design_lapidary_storage", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_source_reader", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_zstd_level_is_the_authority", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_blob_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-phase-1-slice-5-browser-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_zstd_level_is_the_authority", "target": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3b_3mf_design_compression_policy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1